=============\r\n\r\n  -> File: 0913.xlsx (Type: .xlsx)\r\n  -> Reading Excel file: 0913.xlsx\r\n  -> Active sheet: ورقة2\r\n  -> Header row: 6 -> ['أسم العميل', 'أسم الصنف', 'التاريخ', 'الكمية']\r\n  -> Extracted 993 data rows\r\n  -> Auto-detected drug name column: أسم الصنف\r\n  -> Extracted 993 items from column 'أسم الصنف'\r\n     Extracted items: 993\r\n\r\n=================\n<truncated 5906 bytes>\n9. looggggs فين بتاع السسرفر والpipeline\n10. معنى إن الـ loading يظهر في الجزء الشمال، فهو مش يظهر هنا. أولاً، الـ log يظهر تحت الإعدادات، لما أضغط عليه يظهر لي مربع في النص التاني فيه الحاجات اللي بتحصل في الـ terminal. أما في الإعدادات ذات نفسها، في log بتاع الـ server أنت كنت عامله قبل كده وحذفته، راح فين؟ وأنا لما أقول لك الـ loading يبقى الـ pop up على النص الشمال في الحتة اللي أنا عامل لك فيها screenshot. لكن الجزء اليمين اللي هو فيه الإعدادات والجديدة والسجل، ده أقدر أتنقل بينهم براحتي عادي، ولما أجي أتنقل، مثلاً رحت السجل وأرجع مثلاً للجديدة، فالجديدة ديت لسه شغال فيها الـ process اللي أنا لسه مشغلها. في الـ process بتاع الـ shortage\n<truncated 1531 bytes>\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n# Continuation Summary — Pharmacy Matcher Desktop App\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n### Fix Extraction Logic for Varying Formats (Status: DISCOVERY / IMPLEMENTATION)\n- **User's intent**: \"الـ file الأول اللي أنا حاطه مكتوب في الـ extracted 0 items from raw text content... الملف الثاني extracted 4 items... التنسيقات تختلف، الملفات كل مرة هتلاقيها تختلف، ما تبقاش حاطط fixed code، كل حاجه بتتغير.\"\n- **Current State**: The Unstructured API call succeeds, but the post-processing extraction schema in `pdf_reader.py` (and potentially `excel_reader.py`) is too rigid and fails to find drug names in files with different table/text formats.\n- **Next Step**: Review and rewrite the parsing logic in `parse_items_from_response` to be highly robust and adaptive to different PDF layouts.\n\n### UI/UX: Loading Pop-up Placement (Status: IMPLEMENTATION)\n- **User's intent**: \"الـ loading يبقى الـ pop up على النص الشمال في الحتة اللي أنا عامل لك فيها screenshot. لكن الجزء اليمين اللي هو فيه الإعدادات والجديدة والسجل، ده أقدر أتنقل بينهم براحتي عادي\"\n- **Current State**: A floating widget was added to the bottom-left, but the user explicitly wants it positioned properly within the left pane (the \"New Match\" area) as indicated in their screenshot, while keeping the right sidebar navigational.\n- **Next Step**: Adjust CSS for `#progress-modal` to match the user's layout expectations.\n\n### UI/UX: System and Server Logs in Settings (Status: IMPLEMENTATION)\n- **User's intent**: \"الـ log يظهر تحت الإعدادات، لما أضغط عليه يظهر لي مربع في النص التاني فيه الحاجات اللي بتحصل في الـ terminal... في الإعدادات ذات نفسها، في log بتاع الـ server أنت كنت عامله قبل كده وحذفته، راح فين؟\"\n- **Current State**: `sys.stdout` redirection is capturing logs, but the UI presentation in the \"System Settings\" tab is missing or not functioning as the user expects. They want a clickable log section that expands into a terminal view.\n- **Next Step**: Fix the layout of the `#system-logs` textarea in `index.html` under the `#screen-settings` div to match the user's request.\n\n### Restart Failed Processes (Status: NOT STARTED)\n- **User's intent**: \"ولما أقفل البرنامج وأفتحه والـ process ما اكتملش، يبقى فيه زرار في الـ history إن أنا أعمل إعادة تشغيل للـ process بتاعت الـ history كاملة.\"\n- **Current State**: Stuck processes are marked as 'error' on startup, but there is no UI or backend endpoint to restart them.\n- **Next Step**: Add a \"Restart\" button next to \"Delete\" in the History tab and wire it to a new backend method.\n\n### Multi-language UI Support (Status: SUGGESTED)\n- **User's intent**: \"عايز ممكن نضيف لغة ثانية اللي هو الإنجليزي في البرنامج... وتظبط حوار الـ right to left وleft to right\"\n- **Remaining Work**: Postponed to focus on extraction and core stability.\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n\n### Direct User Quotes & Feedback\n- **On File Formats & Extraction:** \"أنت كنت مفكر الملفات متوحدة، أنا قلت لك الملفات تختلف، التنسيقات تختلف، الملفات كل مرة هتلاقيها تختلف، ما تبقاش حاطط fixed code، كل حاجه بتتغير.\"\n- **On UI Layout (Progress Widget):** \"الـ loading يبقى الـ pop up على النص الشمال في الحتة اللي أنا عامل لك فيها screenshot... الجزء اليمين... أقدر أتنقل بينهم براحتي عادي\"\n- **On Logs UI:** \"الـ log يظهر تحت الإعدادات، لما أضغط عليه يظهر لي مربع في النص التاني فيه الحاجات اللي بتحصل في الـ terminal\"\n\n### Context Provided\n- **Screenshot:** Provided an image showing the `progress-modal` floating awkwardly. The user wants it explicitly constrained to the left \"New Match\" content area.\n- **Network Error:** User provided a log showing `[Errno 11001] getaddrinfo failed` for `api.unstructured.io`. This confirmed that the specific DNS doesn't resolve in their environment, requiring the use of `transform.unstructured.io`.\n\n### API Keys & Credentials\n- **MSEMAX API Key**: `[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]` (Server at `D:\\AI_Engineer\\MSEMAX\\`)\n- **Unstructured.io API Key**: stored in project `.env` file at `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\.env`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n\n- **Fixed Unstructured API DNS Error:** Reverted the URL in `pdf_reader.py` from `api.unstructured.io` back to the default `transform.unstructured.io/api/v2/parse` because the former was failing DNS resolution on the user's machine.\n- **Fixed `submitProcess` Argument Type Bug:** Restored `JSON.stringify` around the arrays passed from JS to Python in `index.html`. `pywebview` was automatically converting JS arrays to Python `list`s, which crashed `json.loads` in the backend.\n- **Fixed Process Deduplication Bug:** Modified `start_process` in `backend.py` to properly `json.loads` the `shortage_files` string fetched from SQLite before sorting and comparing it. Previously, it was sorting a raw JSON string character-by-character, causing caching/deduplication to silently fail.\n- **Captured Pipeline Logs (sys.stdout Redirection):** Implemented a `LogRedirector` class in `backend.py` that intercepts all `sys.stdout` and `sys.stderr` output (including all pipeline `print()` statements) and pipes them directly to the JS UI via `new_log` custom events.\n- **Added Pipeline Terminal UI:** Replaced the full-screen blocking `#progress-area` with a `#progress-modal` floating widget containing a mini `#pipeline-log-terminal` that live-streams the backend output. *(Placement still needs UX refinement based on newest feedback).*\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n\n### Architecture & Failures\n- **`pywebview` Data Types:** Passing raw JS arrays to `pywebview.api` methods converts them to Python `list` types. If the Python method expects a JSON string and uses `json.loads()`, it will crash. Always stringify on the JS side.\n- **SQLite Data Retrieval:** Fetching JSON text fields from SQLite via `dict(row)` returns raw `str` objects. They must be explicitly parsed with `json.loads()` in Python before doing array comparisons.\n- **Log Streaming Architecture:** The pipeline workers use standard `print()` statements. By redirecting `sys.stdout` to `self.add_log`, the app seamlessly pushes all background worker logs to the frontend via PyWebView events (`window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('new_log', ...))`).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html`**\n  - *What:* Fixed `JSON.stringify` in `submitProcess`. Changed `#progress-modal` to a floating widget. Added `#pipeline-log-terminal`. Added JS event listeners to pipe `new_log` events to the terminal.\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\backend.py`**\n  - *What:* Added `LogRedirector` to capture `stdout/stderr` in `__init__`. Fixed the duplicate process check in `start_process` to parse DB strings into lists before sorting.\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\extract\\pdf_reader.py`**\n  - *What:* Reverted the `url` assignment to strictly use `transform.unstructured.io/api/v2/parse` to fix user DNS issues.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n**Current Status:** The app successfully launches processes and streams logs to the UI without blocking navigation. However, the data extraction logic inside the pipeline is failing to find items (\"extracted 0 items\"), and the user is unhappy with the exact visual placement of the logs and the progress pop-up.\n\n**Immediate Next Steps:**\n1. **Fix Extraction Logic:**\n   - Open `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\extract\\pdf_reader.py`.\n   - Inspect the `parse_items_from_response` function. \n   - The logic is too rigid (\"fixed code\") and failing to extract items from varying Unstructured JSON responses. Implement a highly robust, fallback-heavy text/table parsing algorithm that can handle varied PDF architectures.\n2. **Implement Restart Button:**\n   - Open `index.html` (JS `updateHistoryUI`) to add a \"Restart\" button next to \"Delete\".\n   - Open `backend.py` to add a `restart_process(process_id)` endpoint that resets the status and spawns a new worker thread.\n3. **Refine UI Placements:**\n   - Open `index.html`.\n   - Ensure the `#system-logs` textarea is visible inside `#screen-settings` and formatted as a collapsible/clickable terminal box.\n   - Adjust `#progress-modal` CSS so it is confined to the left pane (New Match area) instead of `position: fixed` to the bottom of the viewport.\n\nYou have the 23 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/desktop-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:17:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/pharmacy-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T10:46:04Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006220414]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d29166