{"step_index":874,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T00:53:06Z","thinking":"**Considering File Paths**\n\nI'm currently focused on implementing the `restart_process` function within `backend.py`. It needs to update the process status and kick off the thread, but there's a problem: the `processes` table only stores filenames, not full paths. That's a serious roadblock I must address! I need full paths.\n\n\n**Resolving Path Dependencies**\n\nI've realized a workaround! The `restart_process` function in `backend.py` can indeed recover the full file paths. The `_process_worker` function in `backend.py` stores files in `data/inputs/{process_id}`. I now plan to look for the input files there to restart! It is an ideal fallback solution that avoids data loss and will facilitate restarts.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add restart_process in backend.py","EndLine":237,"Instruction":"Add restart_process method to API class","ReplacementContent":"    def restart_process(self, process_id: str) -> dict:\n        try:\n            workspace = PROJECT_ROOT / 'data' / 'inputs' / process_id\n            if not workspace.exists():\n                return {\"success\": False, \"error\": \"ملفات العملية غير موجودة لإعادة التشغيل\"}\n            \n            # get process details\n            cursor = self.db.conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute('SELECT shortage_files, warehouse_files FROM processes WHERE id = ?', (process_id,))\n            row = cursor.fetchone()\n            if not row:\n                return {\"success\": False, \"error\": \"العملية غير موجودة\"}\n                \n            shortage_filenames = json.loads(row['shortage_files'])\n            warehouse_filenames = json.loads(row['warehouse_files'])\n            \n            shortage_paths = [str(workspace / name) for name in shortage_filenames]\n            warehouse_paths = [str(workspace / name) for name in warehouse_filenames]\n            \n            # Reset status\n            self.db.update_process_status(process_id, 'processing')\n            \n            thread = threading.Thread(target=self._process_worker, args=(process_id, shortage_paths, warehouse_paths, True))\n            thread.daemon = True\n            thread.start()\n            \n            return {\"success\": True, \"process_id\": process_id}\n        except Exception as e:\n            return {\"success\": False, \"error\": str(e)}\n\n    def _process_worker(self, process_id: str, shortage_paths: list, warehouse_paths: list, is_restart: bool = False):","StartLine":236,"TargetContent":"    def _process_worker(self, process_id: str, shortage_paths: list, warehouse_paths: list):","TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\backend.py","toolAction":"Add restart_process to backend","toolSummary":"Add restart_process backend"}}]}
